I take it you cannot get out of Sokoban,  have no tool/weapon/wand/
spell to smash/teleport/polymorph boulders, and could not control your
Luck even if outside Sokoban. In this case, I'd probably squeeze
between the boulders and push them from within to somewhere
convenient.

Details: You probably want to start this right before a turn divisible
by 600 to minimize risks. Sokoban has lower monster generation, so
stay safe in there until your bad luck times out. Luck is capped at
-10, you might as well do as many offending actions as you wish. In
particular, you can displace your pet onto the boulder blocking access
to the monster. Then you can play near-pacifist (with lots of
Elbereth) for the rest of Sokoban - you wouldn't hit anything anyway.
(Dogs/cats often die to giant mimics!) It's a matter of taste if you
should anger your god so Luck times out twice as fast. Or you can wait
out the worst of your Luck in an impromptu boulder fort (deposit your
stuff and food, assemble the fort, and squeeze in).

